---
title: Pumpkin Muffins
servings: 12
cuisine: american
main_protein: eggs
prep_time: "45 minutes"
cook_time: "30 minutes"
tags:
  - breakfast
  - pumpkin
  - chocolate
image: ../obsidian/attachments/Pasted image 20260425134052.png
leftover_portions: 8
prep:
  - Soften 0.5 cup butter
  - Preheat oven to 425°F
  - Grease a 12-cup muffin tin
---

Cream @butter{0.5%cup}, softened, and @brown sugar{1%cup} in #mixing bowl{}. Beat in @eggs{2} one at a time until smooth. Stir in @canned pumpkin{1%cup}.

In another bowl combine remaining 9 ingredients: @all-purpose flour{2%cups}, @baking powder{1.5%tsp}, @baking soda{0.5%tsp}, @salt{0.5%tsp}, @cinnamon{0.5%tsp}, @nutmeg{0.5%tsp}, @ground ginger{0.5%tsp}, and @semi-sweet chocolate chips{1%cup}. Stir to mix then pour into mixing bowl. Stir all together just until moistened.

Spoon into #muffin tin{}.

Bake in the #oven{} at 425°F for ~{5%minutes} and then 350°F ~{14%minutes}.

~{10%minutes} cooling time.

-- Yield: 1 loaf
